  "description": [
    {
      "value": "<p>A dressed stone slab with a glass-edged lower lip, dropped into cut grooves at the head of a terrace channel to close a drop between levels. The lip is a strip of volcanic glass set into the stone with silt cement and renewed about once a decade, which is what makes the seal tight enough to stop a channel entirely. This one was replaced in 2286 after the grooves wore out of square, and the wear is heaviest on the left groove face, which is the side the shutter is lifted from. The glass lip is chipped along two thirds of its length and one corner of the slab is missing.</p>",
      "inLanguage": [{ "id": ["core.peerdb.org", "LANGUAGE", "en-GB"] }]
    }
  ],
